WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.329 --> 00:00:03.769
Researcher Ellis was having a very long day.

00:00:03.769 --> 00:00:08.460
Working at the SCP Foundation can sound like
a pretty exciting job to an outsider.

00:00:08.460 --> 00:00:12.650
The problem is, when you deal with something
exciting every day of your life, it starts

00:00:12.650 --> 00:00:17.600
to become as mundane as brushing your teeth,
or pouring your morning bowl of breakfast

00:00:17.600 --> 00:00:18.600
cereal.

00:00:18.600 --> 00:00:21.350
Over time, everything loses its magic.

00:00:21.350 --> 00:00:27.400
She had the unenviable job of double-checking
the anomalies in C-Wing of Site-77.

00:00:27.400 --> 00:00:29.369
Glorified box-ticking.

00:00:29.369 --> 00:00:34.750
She trudged from containment chamber to containment
chamber, everything seeming to be in order.

00:00:34.750 --> 00:00:36.870
Tick, tick, tick.

00:00:36.870 --> 00:00:41.990
It was all Euclid and Safe Class anomalies
anyway, hardly major containment risks.

00:00:41.990 --> 00:00:47.680
But when she reached the chamber for SCP-2805,
the security cameras normally used to observe

00:00:47.680 --> 00:00:49.490
the anomaly were on the fritz.

00:00:49.490 --> 00:00:51.780
She’d need to go inside.

00:00:51.780 --> 00:00:52.780
Great.

00:00:52.780 --> 00:00:55.800
When the chamber doors opened, she felt an
immediate chill.

00:00:55.800 --> 00:00:58.380
Her breath came out as an icy fog.

00:00:58.380 --> 00:01:03.260
In the distance, she saw a jar sitting on
a podium, the glass so frosted over she couldn’t

00:01:03.260 --> 00:01:05.360
quite make out what was inside.

00:01:05.360 --> 00:01:07.420
No sign of a containment breach.

00:01:07.420 --> 00:01:12.800
She ticked the box next to SCP-2805 on her
clipboard, and moved on.

00:01:12.800 --> 00:01:17.710
Several hours later, Researcher Ellis was
at home, finally able to relax.

00:01:17.710 --> 00:01:22.430
Since she started working at the Foundation,
dealing with deadly creatures and cursed artifacts

00:01:22.430 --> 00:01:27.730
on a daily basis, she’d longed for the simple
comforts of childhood in her downtime.

00:01:27.730 --> 00:01:33.030
That’s why she decided to spend her evening
with a warm mug of hot chocolate, a bowl of

00:01:33.030 --> 00:01:37.330
ice cream, and her favorite animated Disney
movie, Mulan.

00:01:37.330 --> 00:01:41.570
She had just pressed play when she got a phone
call from an unknown number.

00:01:41.570 --> 00:01:44.729
With a frustrated groan, she picked up the
phone and answered.

00:01:44.729 --> 00:01:48.620
The voice on the other end was a little gravelly
but it sounded kind.

00:01:48.620 --> 00:01:52.470
His diction was old-fashioned, a man from
a bygone era.

00:01:52.470 --> 00:01:57.790
“Why hello there, young lady, I hope this
isn’t a bad time,” he said.

00:01:57.790 --> 00:01:59.200
“The name’s Walt.

00:01:59.200 --> 00:02:00.350
Walt Disney.

00:02:00.350 --> 00:02:02.780
Perhaps you’ve seen one of my motion pictures.

00:02:02.780 --> 00:02:07.270
I was wondering if I could trouble you for
some help with a project of mine.”

00:02:07.270 --> 00:02:12.180
This must have been some stupid prank call,
maybe Dr. Bright or Dr. Clef was bored and

00:02:12.180 --> 00:02:14.160
decided they wanted to mess with her.

00:02:14.160 --> 00:02:18.600
The fact that she was watching a Disney movie
at the time was pure coincidence.

00:02:18.600 --> 00:02:21.490
After all, they own half the movies out there
these days.

00:02:21.490 --> 00:02:24.290
But that’s when “Walt” carried on talking
to her.

00:02:24.290 --> 00:02:29.890
“You see, my dear, I’m a little short
on time at the moment, I realize I, perhaps,

00:02:29.890 --> 00:02:33.200
um, don’t have the longevity that I used
to.

00:02:33.200 --> 00:02:38.610
I won’t get into the illness right now,
but what I do know is that I may not be able

00:02:38.610 --> 00:02:41.610
to put my final idea into practice.

00:02:41.610 --> 00:02:46.260
And I believe that you, and your organization,
may be able to help.

00:02:46.260 --> 00:02:51.020
Your - what is it called - SCP Foundation?”

00:02:51.020 --> 00:02:53.599
And that changed everything.

00:02:53.599 --> 00:02:57.160
Researcher Ellis immediately knew that this
wasn’t a prank call.

00:02:57.160 --> 00:03:02.660
A member of Foundation staff would never discuss
Foundation matters, even as a joke, over an

00:03:02.660 --> 00:03:04.300
unsecured line.

00:03:04.300 --> 00:03:08.459
And a civilian would have no reason to even
know about the Foundation.

00:03:08.459 --> 00:03:11.430
Was she actually on the phone with the Walt
Disney.

00:03:11.430 --> 00:03:15.470
It seemed odd and more than a little unlikely
on account of him having been dead for over

00:03:15.470 --> 00:03:17.130
fifty years.

00:03:17.130 --> 00:03:20.720
If only Researcher Ellis had checked her clipboard
a little closer.

00:03:20.720 --> 00:03:24.920
Then maybe she would have realized that she
was already under the anomalous effects of

00:03:24.920 --> 00:03:31.390
SCP-2805 - also humorously known as “Disney
on Ice.”

00:03:31.390 --> 00:03:35.400
Here’s a fun question for you: What’s
your favorite Disney movie?

00:03:35.400 --> 00:03:40.000
Probably not what you expected to hear from
your friends at SCP Explained, but seriously,

00:03:40.000 --> 00:03:42.810
we want to know - tell us down in the comments.

00:03:42.810 --> 00:03:46.709
Maybe you’re a classical purist, and you
consider Snow White, Cinderella, or Sleeping

00:03:46.709 --> 00:03:48.380
Beauty to be the best.

00:03:48.380 --> 00:03:51.950
Maybe you’re a fan of the Disney Renaissance,
and it’s The Little Mermaid, Beauty and

00:03:51.950 --> 00:03:55.440
the Beast, or The Lion King tha are the true
masterpieces.

00:03:55.440 --> 00:04:00.030
Or perhaps you’re a fan of their more modern
outings, like Tangled, Frozen, and Moana,

00:04:00.030 --> 00:04:07.099
or even their acquisitions, like Marvel movies
or the Star Wars series.

00:04:07.099 --> 00:04:10.400
We could go on, but honestly, we’d be here
all day.

00:04:10.400 --> 00:04:15.060
The Walt Disney Company, started by Walter
Elias Disney and his brother, Roy, back in

00:04:15.060 --> 00:04:20.600
1923, has become one of the most powerful
and influential entertainment companies in

00:04:20.600 --> 00:04:21.600
existence.

00:04:21.600 --> 00:04:27.370
Their corporate machine is so huge and sprawling,
it rivals the size and scope of the SCP Foundation

00:04:27.370 --> 00:04:32.789
itself, and it’s influenced the way we look
at everything from mice to pirates to Norse

00:04:32.789 --> 00:04:35.139
legends to space battles.

00:04:35.139 --> 00:04:38.801
Some give the United States’ President the
title “Leader of the Free World”, but

00:04:38.801 --> 00:04:43.330
anyone in that position would happily drop
everything to take a phone call from the CEO

00:04:43.330 --> 00:04:46.550
of the Walt Disney Company, even today.

00:04:46.550 --> 00:04:50.860
The company may be a global superpower these
days, but none of it would have been possible

00:04:50.860 --> 00:04:52.699
without Walt himself.

00:04:52.699 --> 00:04:58.219
Born in 1901, Walt started his legendary company
at the tender age of 22.

00:04:58.219 --> 00:05:02.400
Who would have known he would leave such an
indelible mark on human culture during his

00:05:02.400 --> 00:05:04.009
65 years of life.

00:05:04.009 --> 00:05:10.020
But he’s not just an entrepreneur, animator,
writer, voice actor, and film producer, he’s

00:05:10.020 --> 00:05:15.139
also, decades after his death, an anomaly
currently in the capable hands of the SCP

00:05:15.139 --> 00:05:16.139
Foundation.

00:05:16.139 --> 00:05:20.180
Well, his cryogenically frozen severed head
is, anyway.

00:05:20.180 --> 00:05:24.770
And simply looking at that severed head, is
what put such an anomalous damper on Researcher

00:05:24.770 --> 00:05:27.119
Ellis’ nice, quiet evening.

00:05:27.119 --> 00:05:28.119
Confused?

00:05:28.119 --> 00:05:29.119
Don’t worry.

00:05:29.119 --> 00:05:34.739
Let’s start this demented Disney fairytale
at the beginning - by which we mean, The End

00:05:34.739 --> 00:05:36.789
- of Walt Disney’s life.

00:05:36.789 --> 00:05:40.600
Walt Disney accomplished more in his life
than many of us would be able to claim in

00:05:40.600 --> 00:05:41.960
several lifetimes.

00:05:41.960 --> 00:05:47.350
He’d built one of the most enduring entertainment
companies of all time, won countless awards,

00:05:47.350 --> 00:05:52.880
and made millions of dollars from his creations
- including the Disneyland theme parks.

00:05:52.880 --> 00:05:58.349
The man had essentially made his own name
synonymous with magic, childhood whimsy, and

00:05:58.349 --> 00:05:59.610
dreams coming true.

00:05:59.610 --> 00:06:04.999
However, rather than focusing on the past,
Walt wanted to keep his eyes on the future.

00:06:04.999 --> 00:06:10.069
His grand vision went far beyond movies and
theme parks: He wanted to shape the way humanity

00:06:10.069 --> 00:06:12.210
lived for centuries to come.

00:06:12.210 --> 00:06:13.770
And the name of this vision?

00:06:13.770 --> 00:06:17.969
EPCOT, or the Experimental Prototype Community
of Tomorrow.

00:06:17.969 --> 00:06:22.259
While you may know EPCOT as a mere portion
of the theme park in the Florida Walt Disney

00:06:22.259 --> 00:06:26.599
Resort, Walt himself actually intended it
to be so much more.

00:06:26.599 --> 00:06:31.710
As the full name suggests, he dreamed of creating
a functional community of tomorrow, with over

00:06:31.710 --> 00:06:33.309
20,000 residents.

00:06:33.309 --> 00:06:34.479
In his own words:

00:06:34.479 --> 00:06:39.479
"EPCOT will take its cue from the new ideas
and new technologies that are now emerging

00:06:39.479 --> 00:06:42.180
from the creative centers of American industry.

00:06:42.180 --> 00:06:47.149
It will be a community of tomorrow that will
never be completed but will always be introducing

00:06:47.149 --> 00:06:51.270
and testing, and demonstrating new materials
and new systems.

00:06:51.270 --> 00:06:56.389
And EPCOT will always be a showcase to the
world of the ingenuity and imagination of

00:06:56.389 --> 00:06:58.479
American free enterprise."

00:06:58.479 --> 00:07:03.849
It was certainly a utopian idea - though fans
of Bioshock may find their eye twitching with

00:07:03.849 --> 00:07:06.909
flashbacks to Andrew Ryan’s disastrous Rapture.

00:07:06.909 --> 00:07:12.069
However, Disney’s problem didn’t lie in
his plans, but in himself.

00:07:12.069 --> 00:07:17.129
Despite his achievements and larger-than-life
legacy, he was still a mortal man.

00:07:17.129 --> 00:07:22.000
When Walt tragically contracted lung cancer,
he finally became aware of the fact that he

00:07:22.000 --> 00:07:26.240
may not live to see his beautiful EPCOT dream
completed.

00:07:26.240 --> 00:07:30.710
And despite having all the money and fame
a man could possibly ask for, he was beginning

00:07:30.710 --> 00:07:36.979
to realize that his fortune couldn’t buy
him a second of extra time...Or could it?

00:07:36.979 --> 00:07:41.379
This question would soon be answered when
representatives of a mysterious company known

00:07:41.379 --> 00:07:44.360
as The Oneiroi Collective approached Walt.

00:07:44.360 --> 00:07:48.729
The strange thing, though, was that the entities
that comprise this elusive Group of Interest

00:07:48.729 --> 00:07:50.949
contacted Walt in his dreams.

00:07:50.949 --> 00:07:56.869
You see, the Oneiroi Collective are a group
of entities known as the Oneiroi, or Dreamers,

00:07:56.869 --> 00:08:02.189
who exist only in the dreamspace - but sometimes
interact with our world through anomalous,

00:08:02.189 --> 00:08:05.719
sometimes semi-organic creations they sell
as products.

00:08:05.719 --> 00:08:09.439
In that sense, they were the original Imagineers.

00:08:09.439 --> 00:08:14.759
Their creations include SCP-2028, a few hundred
snow globes that allow the user to remove

00:08:14.759 --> 00:08:17.959
and store their nightmares and negative feelings
within.

00:08:17.959 --> 00:08:23.849
And SCP-1498, which are creatures made from
old-fashioned rotary phones trailing a huge

00:08:23.849 --> 00:08:27.999
number of wires, coiled and arranged into
sheep-like bodies.

00:08:27.999 --> 00:08:32.450
By calling the phone on the creature’s face,
a person can order a custom dreamscape from

00:08:32.450 --> 00:08:33.450
the Oneiroi.

00:08:33.450 --> 00:08:38.600
Naturally, as creatures who depend on dreams
to survive, the Oneiroi were big fans of Walt

00:08:38.600 --> 00:08:43.580
Disney - a man who’d built a career on encouraging
children to dream their little hearts out.

00:08:43.580 --> 00:08:48.590
In exchange for his contributions to the Dreamscape,
they’d cut him a deal: They’d give him

00:08:48.590 --> 00:08:52.700
a special kind of Oneiroi technology that
would allow his consciousness to continue

00:08:52.700 --> 00:08:56.700
to exist and interact with the physical realm
after his death.

00:08:56.700 --> 00:08:59.030
All they’d need to keep was his head.

00:08:59.030 --> 00:09:03.940
It was certainly a strange deal, but Walt
was thinking of his children, his grandchildren,

00:09:03.940 --> 00:09:05.940
and their children and grandchildren.

00:09:05.940 --> 00:09:10.040
If he died now, then his Tomorrowland dreams
would die with him.

00:09:10.040 --> 00:09:14.930
He’d simply be known for some charming animated
films and a couple of amusing theme parks,

00:09:14.930 --> 00:09:17.370
not for truly changing the future.

00:09:17.370 --> 00:09:21.100
It seemed that the deal with the Oneiroi Collective
was too good to resist.

00:09:21.100 --> 00:09:25.460
The deal was struck, and arrangements were
made to preserve Disney’s head and consciousness

00:09:25.460 --> 00:09:26.830
after his death.

00:09:26.830 --> 00:09:33.820
Ten days after his 65th birthday, on December
15th, 1966, Walt Disney passed away.

00:09:33.820 --> 00:09:36.860
But that was only the beginning of his new,
anomalous life.

00:09:36.860 --> 00:09:41.160
While the public mourned, Disney’s head
was secretly removed and preserved in a jar

00:09:41.160 --> 00:09:43.700
with anomalous cryonics technology.

00:09:43.700 --> 00:09:48.510
The device is also fixed to a pair of rotary
phones - a trademark of the Oneiroi - and

00:09:48.510 --> 00:09:53.060
an inscription that reads, “Siberian Solutions
from the Oneiroi Collective.”

00:09:53.060 --> 00:09:57.570
The anomalous effect was simple: Anyone who
looked directly at Disney’s frozen head

00:09:57.570 --> 00:10:00.930
would receive a phone call in the next 24
hours.

00:10:00.930 --> 00:10:05.880
This phone call would be from Walt Disney
himself, presumably inhabiting the Oneiroi

00:10:05.880 --> 00:10:06.880
Dreamscape now.

00:10:06.880 --> 00:10:11.240
With this handy trick, he’d be able to maintain
his communications with the rest of the Walt

00:10:11.240 --> 00:10:16.530
Disney Company in secret, and see the creation
of his precious EPCOT project to its completion.

00:10:16.530 --> 00:10:20.300
But unfortunately, that’s not actually how
it happened.

00:10:20.300 --> 00:10:25.240
Following Walt’s “death”, his brother,
Roy, took over all Walt Disney Company operations.

00:10:25.240 --> 00:10:29.851
While the profitability of the company didn’t
suffer under Roy’s control, Walt’s final

00:10:29.851 --> 00:10:31.070
dream did.

00:10:31.070 --> 00:10:36.700
EPCOT mutated from the sustainable, functional
community of the future that Walt desired,

00:10:36.700 --> 00:10:42.270
into a mere theme park - the Disney-fied World’s
Fair that all Orlando Disney park visitors

00:10:42.270 --> 00:10:44.320
of today would recognize.

00:10:44.320 --> 00:10:48.870
As it turned out, most people in the Disney
company weren’t actually eager to take orders

00:10:48.870 --> 00:10:51.590
from the former CEO’s severed head.

00:10:51.590 --> 00:10:57.360
As a result, he became kind of a dark company
secret, hidden away within the Disney parks.

00:10:57.360 --> 00:11:01.630
After a number of reports of calls from Walt
Disney after the entrepreneur's death, the

00:11:01.630 --> 00:11:04.160
Foundation finally started to take notice.

00:11:04.160 --> 00:11:08.500
They conducted a thorough investigation of
the various Disney bases of operation, and

00:11:08.500 --> 00:11:15.300
eventually found Disney’s frozen head - soon
redesignated SCP-2805 - in a secret compartment

00:11:15.300 --> 00:11:18.190
in the legendary Pirates of the Caribbean
ride.

00:11:18.190 --> 00:11:23.410
He was relocated to Site-77 soon after for
further testing, where his anomalous abilities

00:11:23.410 --> 00:11:24.680
were later discovered.

00:11:24.680 --> 00:11:30.820
Sadly for SCP-2805, while his calls to Foundation
staff have all consisted of attempts in enlisting

00:11:30.820 --> 00:11:35.690
the Foundation’s help in making his EPCOT
dreams a reality, nobody has yet taken him

00:11:35.690 --> 00:11:37.200
up on the offer.

00:11:37.200 --> 00:11:41.910
Since his containment, the Foundation’s
main priority has just been suppressing conspiracy

00:11:41.910 --> 00:11:47.320
theories about the existence of Walt Disney’s
cryogenically frozen head, a task which they

00:11:47.320 --> 00:11:50.570
undertake with collaboration from the Disney
company.

00:11:50.570 --> 00:11:55.770
In order to muddy the waters, in 1981, they
began productions of Walt Disney's World on

00:11:55.770 --> 00:12:00.470
Ice, later known as Disney on Ice, a traveling
ice skating show.

00:12:00.470 --> 00:12:04.870
Since then, they also released the incredibly
successful film “Frozen” and its sequel,

00:12:04.870 --> 00:12:09.470
to corrupt any searches for key phrases like
“Disney’s Frozen” or “Walt Ice.”

00:12:09.470 --> 00:12:15.200
It’s been an incredibly effective smokescreen,
as you can probably expect from the SCP Foundation,

00:12:15.200 --> 00:12:20.150
and sadly for Walt and fans of a midcentury
perspective on the future, it’s likely that

00:12:20.150 --> 00:12:23.720
Walt Disney’s dreams will stay within his
disembodied head.

00:12:23.720 --> 00:12:28.740
So if you’re hoping to prove the existence
of this truly wild anomaly, or somehow get

00:12:28.740 --> 00:12:34.340
in contact with Walt and help him to bring
EPCOT to its intended glory, you should probably

00:12:34.340 --> 00:12:36.740
just Let It Go.

00:12:36.740 --> 00:12:43.800
Now go check out “SCP-343 - God” and “A
Sea Snail's Fantasy SCP-1867 - A Gentleman”

00:12:43.800 --> 00:12:47.600
for more SCPs you can have a truly stimulating
conversation with!

